e definition of Hmeasure and the shrinking-scale cover-class inclusion justify unbounded Hscale as δ↓0. N004 has the very same s,δ, so the supremum on F is infinite without any limit-exchange theorem. N001 then supplies hdim(F)≥s+1. S001 exports the fully quantified F001 under D>0 alone, discharging the exponent restriction. S002 uses finite D from N002 to approach D through positive s<D; it closes the only remaining local antecedent D>0. Every direct input is used for a distinct stated purpose.\",\"source_application_check\":\"No M/E is directly used. The N001 instantiations are valid at s>0 and s+1>0; N004 supplies exactly its all-positive-exponent, all-positive-scale inequality. The final passage is an order-density argument for a finite positive D, not an unjustified analytic interchange.\",\"declaration_check\":\"s is a locally arbitrary real in the positive-D branch, with the inequalities explicitly introduced and discharged. Its universally quantified local fact uses the alpha-renamed binder σ, so the exported F001 does not leave a private exponent free. δ appears only under the all-positive-scale assertion. D remains the global extended-real dimension and its finite representative is used only with N002 available.\"},{\"id\":\"R006\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R006/S001-S004 against H001,N001,M006,M007,M008, with no ancestor compactness or interval-dimension assertion imported. S001 gives the complete interval upper bound by mesh 1/N and cost N^{1-a}. S002 proves Σ diam W_i≥1 for arbitrary countable δ-covers via explicitly enlarged open intervals and lets ε↓0 after separating the infinite-cost case. S003 treats zero diameter separately in ρ^s≥δ^{s-1}ρ, has 0<s<1 and δ>0, and proves Hscale≥δ^{s-1}→∞ before taking s↑1. Thus F003 really proves interval dimension one. S004 uses H001 for a point x_0 and proves the map is isometric from the Euclidean distance formula. It then constructs every preimage covering set, compares diameters and