ts. The inspection covered the supplied limiting arguments, the Euclidean diameter estimates, and the measurability conditions for the slicing integral. It also prompted local fixes to declaration scope and empty-cover handling. I’m recording the closing checks before submission; this is author inspection, not independent Audit A acceptance.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0c3f58f1d426e40d016adf5b8a0ac08191ab4cc68275a2e5d8","call_id":"call_dbe0cffb6c0241cea4d1c013ca8e9333","name":"record_author_checks","arguments":"{\"candidate\":6,\"original_context_note\":\"Compared spec.full_target, H001/H002, D001-D006 and D008 against problem.md:14-30 and 34-167. The ambient integer n≥0 is represented by a natural number, with n=0 retained throughout. H001 is precisely the explicitly approved nonemptiness addition in lines 16-23; H002 is the original compactness assumption. Neither a desired conclusion nor a proof claim was promoted to H. Both H are used: H002 in R002/S001 for boundedness and finite covers, H001 in R002/S002 for the singleton case and R006/S004 for x_0. No original H is unused. D001 fixes the closed unit interval; D002 fixes the Euclidean coordinate identification and its exact distance, not the sup product norm. D003/D004 preserve the unnormalized arbitrary-countable-cover formula, nonmeasurable cover members, positive exponents/scales and empty-member zero convention. D008 gives the native Hausdorff-measure operator and full covering formula. D005 is the native extended-nonnegative Hausdorff-dimension supremum definition; the read native definition at HausdorffDimension.lean:96-98 agrees, and the empty-set convention follows from empty covers. D006 defines D without assuming it finite; that property is proved by R002 before any finite-real use. All global definitions are total on their stated domains and require no missing construction guard. The auxiliary B in R002 is explicitly a total real-supremum expression and its bound property is proved, rather than assumed in a choice. The eight retained M sources were positively probed at the pinned commit, their full signatures and ordinary logical axioms inspected, and their actual native source contexts read: Hausdorff.lean:535-552, HausdorffDimension.lean:94-134, Lebesgue/Add.lean:354-367, OuterMeasure/Basic.lean:42-72 and Lebesgue/Basic.lean:85-96. Their NL contracts preserve the EMetricSpace, Borel measurable-space, NNReal exponent, AEMeasurable, Countable and OuterMeasureClass premises as applicable. M009 was an exploratory probe only, is not selected, and supplies no factual use in this proof. The original route is preserved in R002 (ambient bound), R003 (positive-diameter cover preparation and product partitions), R004 (open-interval enlargement and Tonelli slicing), R005 (s↑D), and R006 (length argument for the interval and its isometric copy). All needed constants, cost inequalities and limits from the supplied proof are retained. No material mathematical passage was omitted as optional. The graph has H/E/M-only roots (here no E is selected), one producer for each N/P, and all retained M/N lie in P's AND dependency closure. Structural success is not mathematical certification; these notes report my own actual packet inspection under the shared acceptance criteria.\",\"readiness\":\"no_known_issue\",\"open_issues\":[],\"resolutions\":[],\"output_notes\":[{\"id\":\"N001\",\"note\":\"R001/S001 proves the exact positive-exponent identity Hmeasure=Hnative, including why the native infinite scale changes no supremum and why empty cover members agree. R001/S002 proves all four exported critical-exponent clauses, with the last clause following from the explicit supremum definition. The output quantifies X,A,s and contains the normalization bridge needed by every later dimension argument; no consumer needs the producer body.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"note\":\"R002/S001 establishes boundedness, finite covers at every δ>0 and finite cost for every s>0; R002/S002 supplies the mesh-h box calculation, D≤n, and the separate n=0 singleton proof using H001. Thus the full exported finiteness, real-identification and exceptional-case statements are justified, including the finite Hscale clause needed as the integration constant in R004.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"note\":\"R003/S001 proves the n=0 upper bound without using positive-diameter balls. S002 establishes existence of the required positive-diameter cover; S003 proves the exact 2(√2)^{q+1}ε cost bound at target scale δ; S004 first sends ε to zero, then takes the supremum over δ, and finally sends q down to finite D. The output is the unconditional upper bound hdim(F)≤D+1 in precisely the Euclidean metric.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"note\":\"R004 proves the scale-preserving inequality for every s>0 and δ>0, not only the exponents below D. S001 justifies c<∞, S002-S003 construct measurable open enlargements and the slice cover, S004 establishes c≤Σρ_i^{s+1}+ε, and S005 treats both finite and infinite cover cost before taking infima. The exported formula has both positive-range quantifiers and the same δ on each side, as required by R005.\"},{\"id\":\"N005\",\"note\":\"R005/S001 turns N004 and the infinite Hmeasure(s,E) supplied by N001 into infinite Hmeasure(s+1,F), hence hdim(F)≥s+1 for every 0<s<D. S002 uses the explicitly supplied finite D from N002 to pass s↑D and closes D>0. The exact conditional output is retained, not asserted without its antecedent.\"},{\"id\":\"N006\",\"note\":\"R006/S001-S003 proves hdim(I)=1 by both equal-length upper covers and the complete enlarged-interval length lower bound. S004 derives the cover-pullback inequality for the isometric map t↦(x_0,t), then obtains hdim(F)≥1 and, under the discharged D=0 antecedent, 1=D+1. The output covers n=0 and has no dependence on the private point x_0.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"note\":\"R007/S001 takes only N002,N003,N005,N006: nonnegative finite D has the exhaustive cases D>0 and D=0, each gives the lower bound, and N003 gives the upper bound. Antisymmetry and D=hdim(E) produce exactly spec.conclusion. D002 expands F to the original E×[0,1] with the specified Euclidean identification, so no endpoint, domain or norm conversion is suppressed.\"}],\"inference_notes\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R001/S001-S002 using only M001-M004 and the displayed definitions. S001 compares the actual cover classes and costs at finite scales and observes that the extra r=∞ cover class gives a smaller infimum; this proves the native/raw identity rather than assuming normalization. S002 uses that F001 identity in each separate implication. Its four local antecedents, recorded as L1-L4, are discharged in the same paragraph. The infinite-measure converse uses the displayed supremum definition, not an unlisted dimension theorem. Every direct M has an actual role, and X,A,s are arbitrary on the output's stated domain.\",\"source_application_check\":\"Checked all four application records against the probed signatures. The current metric supplies an extended metric and the Borel σ algebra is chosen explicitly, discharging both structure premises. For M002/M003/M004, s>0 supplies a genuine NNReal exponent. M002 is used only under s<hdim(A); M003 only under hdim(A)<s. In the zero-measure converse, F001 and the local antecedent give Hnative(s,A)=0≠∞ before the M004 conclusion is used. All conclusions are converted back through the equality actually proved in S001.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The locals X,A,s are introduced at S001 and remain in scope through S002; s has the positive-real domain of N001. Cover families and scale variables inside M001's infima/suprema are expression-bound. Native Hnative and hdim have the extended-metric domains matching their sources; Hmeasure/Hscale are used only on the current ordinary metric space and positive arguments. No witness or branch assumption escapes.\"},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R002/S001-S002 with H001,H002,N001 as the exact direct inputs. Compactness is unfolded as finite open subcovers: the integer-radius ball cover proves boundedness and a radius-δ/2 ball cover proves finite cost. The finite family is made nonempty before taking a maximum, so the argument does not accidentally use H001 in S001. F001 supplies the actual norm bound to the grid calculation. S002 counts at most (2B/h+3)^n≤(2B+3)^n h^{-n} cubes, uses their Euclidean √n h diameter, and uses a>n to get h^{a-n}→0. At every fixed scale this proves zero Hmeasure, so N001 yields D≤a for all a>n and then D≤n. The n=0 branch uses H001 to identify E with the ambient singleton and closes separately. The two n-branches are exhaustive and discharged.\",\"source_application_check\":\"No M/E is directly applied in this packet; N001 is a conditional input with its full normalized critical-exponent conclusions. It is instantiated only at positive a>n in the positive-ambient branch and positive s in the singleton branch. The exponent-power limits are ordinary one-variable positive-power limits with a-n>0 explicitly available, not a hidden cover or dimension theorem.\",\"declaration_check\":\"B is a total explicit real expression introduced in S001; boundedness is proved before its least-upper-bound property is invoked, and B≥1 is shown. δ,s are arbitrary positive parameters only for the finite-cover paragraph and are universally closed; the exported F001 alpha-renames them δ_0,s_0. The grid variables a,h and constant C are introduced in S002 with n>0, a>n, 0<h≤1 and C=(2B+3)^n. Grid indices and x in the norm bound are bound variables. No chosen finite subcover or mesh-dependent cube is exported as a global object.\"},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R003 against only N001,N002. N002 supplies finiteness/nonnegativity of D and the n=0 singleton identification. S001 explicitly uses interval subdivisions when n=0. In the n≥1 branch q>D implies q>0; zero Hmeasure and the infimum definition give a cover of cost <ε/2. The singleton replacement has positive diameter in this branch and adds at most Σ ε2^{-i-2}=ε/2, proving F001 before any cover witness is chosen. S003 uses 0<r_i≤1 to justify ceil(1/r_i)≤2/r_i, the Euclidean distance for √2 r_i, and the exact cost sum. S004's limiting order is correct: arbitrary ε, arbitrary δ, then q↓D; the cover may depend on ε but the bound for Hscale does not. L1 is closed in S001 and the positive-dimensional/restricted-parameter assumptions L2,L3 are discharged in S004.\",\"source_application_check\":\"There is no direct M/E call. N001 is used first to obtain Hmeasure(q,E)=0 from q>D, and later to deduce hdim(F)≤q+1 from the zero measure proved by the product cover; all exponents are positive. Its use in S001 similarly has a>1. Positive-radius Euclidean balls, real-power limits, countability of a countable family of finite partitions, and the geometric-series cost are routine background steps with their actual positivity/countability conditions displayed; no missing substantive product-dimension theorem is invoked.\",\"declaration_check\":\"Read the actual U witness introduction in S003: it cites the earlier complete F001 from S002. The sequences r_i,N_i and products T are defined only after U and remain within that branch. q,δ,ε,r are live S002-S004 with all parameter dependencies explicit; r>0 and r≤1,δ/√2 follow from δ>0. N,a,δ_0 are confined to the n=0 paragraph. Expression indices i,j are bound in their sums/finite partitions. No cover, replacement ball or private local parameter appears in the exported upper bound.\"},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected S001-S005 as the actual slicing argument, using only N002,M005,M007,M008. N002 supplies finite Hscale at the chosen positive s,δ, so c is finite before integration. S002 derives the two projection diameter bounds from the Euclidean distance formula; the nonempty projected B_i is bounded, so its sup/inf construction has the asserted endpoints and gives length ≤ρ_i+η_i. Empty padding has ρ_i^s=0 and J_i=∅. S003 proves coverage at every t∈I and measurability of each indicator term; arbitrary covering sets themselves are never assumed measurable. In S004 the integral is a nonnegative extended integral, so Tonelli applies without integrability or finite-series assumptions. The coefficient estimate η_iρ_i^s≤ε2^{-i-1}, followed by the geometric sum, proves exactly c≤Σρ_i^{s+1}+ε. S005 handles infinite cover cost separately and only then sends ε to zero in the finite case; c and cover cost are independent of ε. Taking the infimum over arbitrary covers has the correct inequality direction. All restrictions L1,L2 and the universal s,δ choices are closed.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M005 is instantiated with α=ℝ, its Borel structure, μ=volume restricted to I, β=ℕ and f_i(t)=ρ_i^s1_{J_i}(t). F003 is an earlier displayed proof of measurability, giving AEMeasurable for this measure. This matches the exact source, which requires countability and AE measurability, not Bochner integrability. M007 with endpoints 0,1 gives mass(I)=1. M008 uses the finite endpoints proved in S002 and η_i>0; the empty case is handled separately. Measure monotonicity gives |J_i∩I|≤|J_i|. Computing ∫_I f_i as ρ_i^s|J_i∩I| is the measurable simple-function integral formula, with J_i∩I Borel and finite nonnegative coefficient; thus the measure/domain change after Tonelli is justified.\",\"declaration_check\":\"s,δ,ε,c are introduced in S001 and live to S005. V is an arbitrary δ-cover, not an unjustified chosen witness. ρ,A_i,B_i,η,J are explicitly defined in S002 in dependency order; the claims needed about finite endpoints are proved there before their interval properties are used. f is introduced in S003 and its exact formula is exported in F003. Indices in sequences/sums and slice variables t,x are bound in their stated quantifiers. The local epsilon-dependent J is eliminated from the final formula. No finiteness or measurable-cover premise is smuggled into a definition.\"},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R005/S001-S002 using just N001,N002,N004. Under the local D>0 and 0<s<D conditions, N001 gives infinite Hmeasure(s,E). The definition of Hmeasure and the shrinking-scale cover-class inclusion justify unbounded Hscale as δ↓0. N004 has the very same s,δ, so the supremum on F is infinite without any limit-exchange theorem. N001 then supplies hdim(F)≥s+1. S001 exports the fully quantified F001 under D>0 alone, discharging the exponent restriction. S002 uses finite D from N002 to approach D through positive s<D; it closes the only remaining local antecedent D>0. Every direct input is used for a distinct stated purpose.\",\"source_application_check\":\"No M/E is directly used. The N001 instantiations are valid at s>0 and s+1>0; N004 supplies exactly its all-positive-exponent, all-positive-scale inequality. The final passage is an order-density argument for a finite positive D, not an unjustified analytic interchange.\",\"declaration_check\":\"s is a locally arbitrary real in the positive-D branch, with the inequalities explicitly introduced and discharged. Its universally quantified local fact uses the alpha-renamed binder σ, so the exported F001 does not leave a private exponent free. δ appears only under the all-positive-scale assertion. D remains the global extended-real dimension and its finite representative is used only with N002 available.\"},{\"id\":\"R006\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R006/S001-S004 against H001,N001,M006,M007,M008, with no ancestor compactness or interval-dimension assertion imported. S001 gives the complete interval upper bound by mesh 1/N and cost N^{1-a}. S002 proves Σ diam W_i≥1 for arbitrary countable δ-covers via explicitly enlarged open intervals and lets ε↓0 after separating the infinite-cost case. S003 treats zero diameter separately in ρ^s≥δ^{s-1}ρ, has 0<s<1 and δ>0, and proves Hscale≥δ^{s-1}→∞ before taking s↑1. Thus F003 really proves interval dimension one. S004 uses H001 for a point x_0 and proves the map is isometric from the Euclidean distance formula. It then constructs every preimage covering set, compares diameters and costs, and takes the actual infimum/supremum to establish the monotonicity needed here. Infinite interval measure for a∈(0,1) is supplied by N001 and F003, not merely guessed from an embedding. D=0 is discharged, and this proof never requires n>0.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M006 is applied to the family J_i with index ℕ and Lebesgue measure in the canonical type of measures on Borel ℝ; these measures have the native FunLike and OuterMeasureClass structures, and no measurability of W_i is needed. M007 at 0,1 gives volume I=1. M008 at the displayed finite inf/sup enlargement endpoints gives length at most ρ_i+ε2^{-i-1}, including singleton members; empty members are handled by zero measure. N001 is used at a>1 for the upper bound, at 0<s<1 for the interval lower bound, and then at 0<a<1 in the embedded copy argument. All exponents and cover-scale domains agree.\",\"declaration_check\":\"N,a in S001 and δ,ε,W,ρ,J in S002 have confined scopes. S002's closed cover assertion F002 uses δ_0,W_0, avoiding the current paragraph locals. S003 has its own s,δ_1,W_1,ρ_1. In S004 the witness x_0 has the explicit direct existence basis H001; φ is then defined with this point, and its range and isometry are proved from E×I and its metric. The arbitrary b,δ_2,Q and the explicit Qpre cover are confined to that pullback argument. The later a∈(0,1) is a different scoped binding from S001's a>1. Only the dimension inequality is exported, so neither x_0 nor the covers escape.\"},{\"id\":\"R007\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the single final paragraph with direct inputs N002,N003,N005,N006 only. N002 provides nonnegative finite D; the cases D>0 and D=0 are exhaustive. Each conditional lower-bound input is used only in its own case, and both case assumptions L1,L2 are discharged. N003 supplies the reverse bound. Antisymmetry plus unfolding D and F yields the exact target; no producer fact or extra original H is read into this packet.\",\"source_application_check\":\"No M/E application occurs. N005 and N006 are instantiated with the very same global D and F and their antecedents are the displayed respective branch assumptions. N003 is the unconditional upper bound, and N002 licenses the finite-real interpretation used in the split.\",\"declaration_check\":\"There are no new mathematical objects or witnesses. D,F,E,n,hdim are globally declared with full definitions in this packet. The two case antecedents are local and closed. The coordinate identification and interval endpoints are available through D002 and D001 rather than an absent producer body.\"}]}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"arr